  "body": "Both HTML demos now functionally implement the **browser-feasible** parts of the Gen-4 reproductive/symbiotic tissue as Body primitives (the established `ZOMBIE_PRIMITIVES` pattern), reusing the genesis key from the self/other work. Faithful to the `mantle/` framework:\n\n- **MEM plasmid** \u2014 `mem.excrete` (a **keyless**, portable knowledge blob \u2014 a \"USB stick\", not an organism) / `mem.digest` (ingest an OTHER plasmid \u2192 re-derive entries as **inferred** with provenance `foreign-MEM`; **refuse** anything carrying a genesis key \u2014 that would be an organism).\n- **Seed vault** \u2014 `vault.seal` / `vault.reconstruct`: the genome sealed with a MAC bound to **SELF**; only the sealing body's key reopens it (an OTHER body cannot reconstruct).\n- **Egg** \u2014 `egg.author` (a whole AppAI declared as **data**) / `egg.hatch` (validate the required tissue, then instantiate a fresh organism's genome; an incomplete egg is refused).\n- **Ganglia \u2248 the Arms** (already present): labeled as such in the `ORGAN_ATLAS`.\n\nThe parts that act on a real **host repo** \u2014 host residency (`anchor`), the **graft egg**, and the self-redesigning **compiler** \u2014 are inherently out of reach for a single-page demo and are marked **framework-only** (they live in `mantle/`). The MIND's `reflexExecBinding` catalog (Reference Agent enum + both `ZOMBIE_PRIMITIVES` allow-lists) and the `ORGAN_ATLAS` (Genome/Memory/Limbs) now list all of these. `examples/README` + PRIMER updated; the headless smoke test (`examples/tests`) asserts the new primitives are present and functional in **both** demos.\n\n## Verified\n- Both demos: keyless plasmid digested as inferred, keyed \"plasmid\" rejected, **SELF-gated vault** (OTHER cannot open), egg hatches into a banded organism, incomplete egg refused; Spreadsheet self-audit PASS; Reference Agent mounts clean.\n- Headless `DEMO SMOKE PASSED` (extended with the new assertions); `python -m mantle prove` \u2192 **68/68 green**.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
